WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.199
Stop!

2
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.919
Require assistance!
Assistance required!

3
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.680
Stop where you are!

4
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.759
Stay away from me!

5
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.559
Stop where you are! Stop!

6
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.639
Get off. get off!

7
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.679
Argh! Get off me! Stop!

8
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.239
I told her! No-one listens!
Can you... can you get off me?!

9
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.280
Get off me or you'll die too!

10
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.319
He will not speak
on his own authority!

11
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.599
He will tell you of things to come!

12
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.520
Terrible. terrible things to come!

13
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.279
No! No. no. Dad!

14
00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.759
No. no! NO! Dad! No!

15
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.080
No!

16
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.879
Follow my finger.

17
00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.879
Two. Three. Four.

18
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.839
Now close your eyes.

19
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.440
What do you see?

20
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.719
{\an8}Pulling the curtain round the bed.
for privacy.

21
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.279
Can you hear the doctor's voice?

22
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.519
Saying something about...

23
00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.239
...nerve damage.

24
00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.759
How do you feel?

25
00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.600
Like I'm going to throw up.

26
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.840
Because I can't feel my legs.

27
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.279
I can see the nurse.
A sad sympathy face.

28
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.800
{\an8}I hate it.

29
00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:29.831
- Oh. my God!

30
00:02:29.832 --> 00:02:32.719
- Never seen a mermaid
get out of a pool before?

31
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.359
Inhale.

32
00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.879
Two. three. four.

33
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.240
and hold.

34
00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.239
Now let's come back.

35
00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.080
Three. four and...

36
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.119
{\an8}...finish.

37
00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.680
{\an8}Take a moment.

38
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.759
Good work today. Gabs. OK?

39
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.559
Yeah. It's hard.

40
00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.480
but it helps.

41
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.599
How are you feeling
about your first shift?

42
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.720
Oh...

43
00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.920
Work always made me
feel alive. so...

44
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.200
I'm good at what I do.
I want to get that feeling back.

45
00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:33.599
OK. well.

46
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.439
high stress can flare up PTSD.

47
00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.679
I know you know that.

48
00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.719
Just be aware of the triggers. OK?

49
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.199
Therapist to therapist.

50
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.640
I'm ready.

51
00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.079
Good morning!

52
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.159
You're listening
to Radio South Wales.

53
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.599
It's shaping up
to be another scorcher out there.

54
00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.679
The mercury is set to break
40 degrees today.

55
00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.319
so a reminder to keep hydrated

56
00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.719
and stay inside
during the hottest part of the day.

57
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.599
Activist group The Climate Front
are warning temperatures like these

58
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.239
are only likely to continue.

59
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.239
This really is starting to feel like
a never-ending summer.

60
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.239
isn't it. John? I can barely think
straight in this heat.

61
00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.280
Hi. it's Dr Gabrielle Fox
for the Child and Adolescent unit.

62
00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.559
Is it always so hot in here?

63
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.639
No aircon. Temperatures rise.
but budgets fall.

64
00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.919
Oh. um. there's the therapy room.

65
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.400
the rec room...

66
00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.480
...and this is your office.

67
00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.119
Oh. um. just a little bit
of light reading.

68
00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:42.840
- Oh. great.

69
00:04:42.841 --> 00:04:45.719
- Yeah. if you can
familiarise yourself with that.

70
00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.959
There's a staff briefing
in about an hour.

71
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:53.039
Oh. and. um. Dr Fox.
welcome to Oxsmith.

72
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.519
It's really great
to have you on board.

73
00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.000
Thanks.

74
00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:24.799
Let's start with
the highest needs. Yeah?

75
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.319
- Bethany Krall.
- Daughter of Leonard - The Faith Way guy.

76
00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.159
Killed her own mother
with a screwdriver in the eye.

77
00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.439
Quite chilling.

78
00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.399
Fortunately.
child protection prevented

79
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.679
any of the gruesome details
from leaking.

80
00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.439
OK. Er. my predecessor's reports
are surprisingly minimal.

81
00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.839
Did she leave any additional
notes anywhere?

82
00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.159
Not to my knowledge.
Dr Ehmet?

83
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.080
No. Afraid not.

84
00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.399
I assume she's under a Section 41?

85
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.839
Yeah. no release without approval
from a tribunal

86
00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.959
- or a Ministry of Justice.
- And treatment-wise?

87
00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.679
She's on anti-psychotics. mostly.
Sometimes lorazepam for sedation.

88
00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.519
- if she's being particularly violent.
- And is she?

89
00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.359
Yeah. there have been
a few incidents.

90
00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.359
She often needs to be restrained.
We try to make that a last resort.

91
00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.360
but she has injured
several members of staff.

92
00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.239
Does Leonard Krall visit?

93
00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.679
He spends a lot of time
on the road at his churches.

94
00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.919
But he does come back here
at least once a month.

95
00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.559
and he always makes
a request to see her.

96
00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.279
Always refused by Bethany.

97
00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.079
Mm. Yes.

98
00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.359
Oh. Rafiq is Bethany's
main nurse contact.

99
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.959
He has a good rapport with her

100
00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.279
and will usually be present
in her sessions.

101
00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.760
What do you make of her. Rafiq?

102
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.320
She's very smart.

103
00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:43.719
OK. so moving on.
Emily Baxter.

104
00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.679
Right. agoraphobia
and chronic anxiety.

105
00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:47.840
Emily?

106
00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.360
I'm Dr Fox.

107
00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.080
You can call me Gabs.

108
00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.039
How do you feel about coming
to the therapy room for a session?

109
00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.120
Switch off
and pretend we're not doomed.

110
00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.240
Is that what YOU do?

111
00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.600
Sometimes. yeah.

112
00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.039
Simon Keegan -
goes by the name Sonic.

113
00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.399
Emotional dysregulation.
complete lack of impulse control.

114
00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.319
I see from your notes
that you like puzzles. Sonic.

115
00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.639
so I bought this one

116
00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.640
in case it helps
to have something to focus on?

117
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.480
Have you met her yet. miss?

118
00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.920
It's today. isn't it?

119
00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.200
Yes. today.

120
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.559
Wait.

121
00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.919
I want to close my eyes.

122
00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.240
Bethany. come on. No games.

123
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.000
Right...

124
00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.320
You ready?

125
00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.400
Hiya.

126
00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.280
No. this is wrong.

127
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.119
Are you expecting someone else?

128
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:19.039
I knew you had a car crash -
I didn't know you were a cripple.

129
00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.119
Bethany...

130
00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.560
No. it's OK.

131
00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.199
I'm your new clinical psychologist.
Dr Fox.

132
00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.640
You can call me Gabs.

133
00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.680
And I prefer "wheelchair user".

134
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.120
Uh...

135
00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.240
You start with five stars.

136
00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.519
- Five stars?
- OK...

137
00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.679
...you can have six.

138
00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.240
Positive discrimination
and all that.

139
00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.679
And what are these stars for?

140
00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.679
Intelligent psychological practice.

141
00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.680
- Mm!
- I'm serious.

142
00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.279
I have seen so many of you.

143
00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.119
Session one - gain
the patient's trust. Textbook.

144
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.319
If you can do that

145
00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.679
without losing your stars...

146
00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:08.880
{\an8}...I might let you
see me again.

147
00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.279
And how can I gain your trust?

148
00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:12.879
By not asking stupid questions.

149
00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.839
And what constitutes
a stupid question?

150
00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.920
That. You lose a star.

151
00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.399
What would you like to talk about?

152
00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:22.839
How about you wearing make-up.

153
00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.759
even though no-one's going to look
at you like that ever again?

154
00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.640
Thought the last shrink was tragic.

155
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.600
Dr Morgan?

156
00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:36.439
- Mm-hm.
- Your previous psychologist.

157
00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.480
Ugh...

158
00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.399
You seem angry. Bethany.

159
00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.639
Yeah. of course I'm angry.
I'm in prison.

160
00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.039
That's a star
for the dumbest question yet.

161
00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.720
It's not a prison. it's a hospital.

162
00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.080
- Are you afraid of me?
- Bethany...

163
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.199
Are YOU afraid of you?

164
00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.919
Ugh!

165
00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.679
That's another star. Three left.

166
00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.760
Choose your words wisely. Wheels.

167
00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:13.239
Do you like to set the parameters
of all your conversations. Bethany?

168
00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.959
Does it make you feel powerful?

169
00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.599
Stop flirting with me.

170
00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:20.200
Or perhaps. by making this exchange
a test. it allows you to control it.

171
00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:27.760
How can I help you feel safe?

172
00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:32.279
Two tiny stars left for Dr Wheels.

173
00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.000
Are you flirting with ME now?

174
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.359
You been swimming?

175
00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.519
Do I smell of chlorine?

176
00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:46.959
No.

177
00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.120
Just desperation.

178
00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:55.079
You probably spend every night
on your own.

179
00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:58.400
stalking people
you used to know online.

180
00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.120
Bethany.

181
00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.080
Your dad's big on the internet.
isn't he?

182
00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.480
Are you. um. like. 100 years old?

183
00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.319
He's an influencer. yeah.

184
00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.719
The "choose hope" guy.
Tell me about him.

185
00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.320
Family! That's very original.

186
00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.400
That is another star.

187
00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.759
And when did you lose trust
in your dad?

188
00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.640
When he believed I killed my mum.

189
00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:34.199
And you didn't?

190
00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.119
You have my files.

191
00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.720
Read them.

192
00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.239
Uh...!

193
00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.999
And she's out.

194
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.840
Well. then. Thank you.

195
00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:50.720
Rafiq?

196
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.719
- Yes.
- What. that's it?

197
00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:56.159
Giving up already?

198
00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:57.879
You can decide
if you want to see me again.

199
00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.000
Hands.

200
00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:21.720
{\an8}The more depressing
the world feels...

201
00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.240
I'm Leonard Krall...

202
00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:36.999
We have 278 affiliated centres
across the UK.

203
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.879
And for those of you
new to religion.

204
00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.640
when I talk about God.
I mean a higher power...

205
00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:48.319
But knowing that we're guided
by something greater than ourselves

206
00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.320
allows us to have hope.

207
00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.039
Yeah. there's one patient.

208
00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.200
She seemed to know things about me.

209
00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:48.080
Well. about the crash.

210
00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.480
A lucky guess. perhaps?

211
00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.639
How did it make you feel?

212
00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.760
Angry. actually.

213
00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:02.320
Yeah. Like - that's mine.
don't come near it.

214
00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:06.439
Guess I forgot what it's like

215
00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.239
to sit. day in. day out.
with other people's trauma.

216
00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.600
I'm fine. It's just a job.

217
00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.119
I used to have a pretty good system
for all this.

218
00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.639
I'd go for a run.
and if that didn't work.

219
00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.599
I'd seduce Alex
and shag the frustration out.

220
00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.320
Is that something you miss?

221
00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:24.960
I can't imagine...

222
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.799
Oh. I feel totally cut off
from that part of myself now.

223
00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:32.440
I can't imagine anyone
but Alex ever touching me.

224
00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.600
Or if I'd even feel it if they did.

225
00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.640
Did you speak to your sister?

226
00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.720
She's busy. I'm busy.

227
00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.799
And what about the group events
at the spinal unit?

228
00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:46.959
Did you join any?

229
00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:50.639
I couldn't bring myself to.
They all look too... happy.

230
00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:53.119
Yeah. one of them wears
a "Choose Hope" T-shirt.

231
00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.079
and that is my litmus test
for twats.

232
00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.559
Loneliness is very real. Gabrielle.

233
00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:01.880
Not having a single person nearby
who you can talk to isn't healthy.

234
00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:05.160
I have you.

235
00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:16.919
Hi. All right? Sorry.
you've just really got to jab at it.

236
00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:18.199
Oh!

237
00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.679
I'm going back in with Bethany now.

238
00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.159
Is it possible
to contact her previous psych.

239
00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.999
see if she's got any paper notes?

240
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:25.679
Er. do you have a number?

241
00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:28.279
Um. Dr Morgan's
had some health problems.

242
00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.359
so I'm not sure
that would be appropriate.

243
00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.679
- Ah.
- Oh. there you go.

244
00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:33.800
Thanks.

245
00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.920
You know it doesn't work inside.

246
00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:46.199
One step at a time. Bethany. hmm?

247
00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.359
Hey.

248
00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:48.599
Wheels!

249
00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.560
Woo-ooo!

250
00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:53.679
Trying to win me over?

251
00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.120
Am I trying to gain
your trust? Yeah.

252
00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.079
Do you want draw something for me?

253
00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:06.119
What. and then you analyse
my scribbles?

254
00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.599
No.

255
00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.800
Well. drawing can be a good way
of bypassing the conscious mind.

256
00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:15.400
Circumventing verbal defences.

257
00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:19.080
Told you.
I've seen a lot of shrinks.

258
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.280
Too many walls.

259
00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:32.719
I get messages from the earth.

260
00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.159
I need to be outside
to receive them.

261
00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.599
What kind of messages
does the earth send?

262
00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:39.639
Visions...

263
00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.480
...of the future.

264
00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.200
