339
00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:07.800
Uh. red. please.

340
00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:10.559
No. then.

341
00:24:17.480 --> 00:24:18.960
Thank you.

342
00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:43.639
Nice to meet you. too.

343
00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:46.919
Hi. Dick Carwyn. Porth Hen Gazette.

344
00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:49.799
How do you feel about
the new wind farm - for or against?

345
00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:51.879
Oh. I'm just here for the free wine.

346
00:24:51.880 --> 00:24:53.839
I know nothing about all this.

347
00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:56.760
The white is undrinkable.
even for me.

348
00:24:58.120 --> 00:25:00.359
Hey. you work at Oxsmith?

349
00:25:00.360 --> 00:25:01.639
Yeah.

350
00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:03.879
That's where Bethany Krall
is. right?

351
00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:06.239
I can't talk about anyone
at the hospital.

352
00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:08.719
There are laws - as well you know.

353
00:25:08.720 --> 00:25:12.279
I wrote several pieces on
the Kralls. back when I wrote

354
00:25:12.280 --> 00:25:15.159
real articles for a real newspaper.

355
00:25:15.160 --> 00:25:18.760
Condemned to
the Porth Hen Gazette now.

356
00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:21.599
How is that still a thing?

357
00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:24.159
I've got a Substack.
but even less people read that.

358
00:25:24.160 --> 00:25:25.759
and they pay zilch.

359
00:25:25.760 --> 00:25:27.559
Well. check it out.

360
00:25:27.560 --> 00:25:30.000
- Oh. wait.
- Wait. watch it.

361
00:25:31.200 --> 00:25:33.160
Darling. is this man bothering you?

362
00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:36.880
No... my love.

363
00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:39.920
He was just leaving.

364
00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:45.080
Well. you've got my details
if you want to talk.

365
00:25:46.280 --> 00:25:48.200
I know a lot about the Krall family.

366
00:25:50.200 --> 00:25:53.199
- Local hack.
- Yeah. he's... he's been doing the rounds.

367
00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:54.559
He's a nuisance.

368
00:25:56.480 --> 00:25:58.639
So are you part of all this. then?

369
00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:00.280
Yeah. 'Fraid so.

370
00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:05.559
I'm trying to think
of something intelligent to ask.

371
00:26:05.560 --> 00:26:08.399
Oh. thank God. You don't give a shit
about any of this. do you?

372
00:26:08.400 --> 00:26:11.039
I work for the NHS -
can't afford our own booze.

373
00:26:11.040 --> 00:26:12.439
- OK!
- Gabs.

374
00:26:12.440 --> 00:26:14.719
- Oh. Frasier. Hi.
- Hi.

375
00:26:14.720 --> 00:26:16.519
Yeah. my God. I'm done too. I think.

376
00:26:16.520 --> 00:26:18.919
Handshakes. speeches.
photos - check.

377
00:26:18.920 --> 00:26:21.999
- Time to go. I'm starving.
- Yeah. I thought there'd be proper food.

378
00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.599
So did I!

379
00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:26.319
Um. I'm actually going for a pizza
if you wanted to join.

380
00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:28.319
Oh. no. thanks.

381
00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:31.119
Pizza might be your code word
for "axe".

382
00:26:31.120 --> 00:26:33.439
Yeah. can't be too careful!

383
00:26:33.440 --> 00:26:35.399
Yeah. thanks for the offer.
but. um...

384
00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:37.599
Sorry if that was. um.
weirdly forward.

385
00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:39.599
I've just. um...
I just moved here recently.

386
00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:41.680
so I don't really know anyone. Um...

387
00:26:42.720 --> 00:26:44.560
But you probably have
actual friends.

388
00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:48.039
Bloody mad!

389
00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:50.000
You know. you know.
pizza sounds great.

390
00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:52.959
- Yeah?
- Mm-hm.

391
00:26:52.960 --> 00:26:54.439
- OK.
- Mm-hm.

392
00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:57.239
Give me that.
Pizza sounds great! This way.

393
00:26:57.240 --> 00:26:59.640
Oh. shit. where did I put that axe?

394
00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:18.879
So. what brings you to Porth Hen?

395
00:27:18.880 --> 00:27:21.039
I take it you're not
from here either.

396
00:27:21.040 --> 00:27:22.799
- Uh. Manchester.
- Mm.

397
00:27:22.800 --> 00:27:25.359
But Cardiff has
a great spinal recovery unit.

398
00:27:25.360 --> 00:27:28.599
so I originally moved
to be near that.

399
00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:30.879
- I had a car accident.
- I'm sorry.

400
00:27:30.880 --> 00:27:32.279
And...

401
00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:34.559
...then I got a job at Oxsmith.

402
00:27:34.560 --> 00:27:36.839
- so I decided to stay.
- OK.

403
00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:39.520
It must be hard being away
from... hometown.

404
00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:43.120
Actually. it's easier this way.

405
00:27:44.800 --> 00:27:47.439
Hard to be around people
with unchanged lives.

406
00:27:47.440 --> 00:27:48.560
It's...

407
00:27:50.200 --> 00:27:52.199
I miss my sister.

408
00:27:52.200 --> 00:27:55.440
But she's on baby number three.
so. you know. busy.

409
00:27:58.800 --> 00:28:00.319
How about you?

410
00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:03.759
Um. I just relocated for this job.

411
00:28:03.760 --> 00:28:06.279
I'm a geologist by trade. but I. um.

412
00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:09.000
I transferred from the London office
to work on the wind farm.

413
00:28:10.040 --> 00:28:12.559
So is it true
what The Climate Front is saying?

414
00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:13.959
And the protesters?

415
00:28:13.960 --> 00:28:16.039
Trenmoor still has a load
of oil sites?

416
00:28:16.040 --> 00:28:18.519
Yeah. they do.
but all UK drilling has stopped.

417
00:28:18.520 --> 00:28:22.399
And. I mean. you can't
just go green globally overnight.

418
00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:26.039
I'm all for activism. but I think
protesting a wind farm event

419
00:28:26.040 --> 00:28:28.119
is maybe a little overzealous.

420
00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:30.600
To be honest.
I mainly switch the news off.

421
00:28:31.680 --> 00:28:35.120
Been more focused on saving myself
than the planet.

422
00:28:36.240 --> 00:28:37.680
Tell me about that.

423
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:40.319
This isn't a date. you know.

424
00:28:40.320 --> 00:28:41.400
Of course not.

425
00:28:42.440 --> 00:28:46.719
No. I mean. I only date
geological matter anyway.

426
00:28:46.720 --> 00:28:48.600
Sorry!

427
00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:54.920
Ah. thank you.

428
00:29:06.840 --> 00:29:08.959
Hi. Gabs. Uh. dinner tonight?

429
00:29:08.960 --> 00:29:10.959
And I can cook.
if you're still up for it?

430
00:29:10.960 --> 00:29:12.760
Seven? I'll bring the wine.

431
00:29:37.440 --> 00:29:40.399
Having one new green project
in the UK does not make up

432
00:29:40.400 --> 00:29:43.839
for their 76 oil sites
around the world.

433
00:29:43.840 --> 00:29:48.199
Trenmoor's Porth Hen wind farm
is a classic greenwashing exercise.

434
00:29:48.200 --> 00:29:52.039
and they are still lobbying to open
a new oil site in the North Sea.

435
00:29:52.040 --> 00:29:54.439
The Rostyre field was only halted

436
00:29:54.440 --> 00:29:57.079
by a legal case
launched by The Climate Front.

437
00:29:57.080 --> 00:30:00.240
We need to come together to change
the system. not the climate.

438
00:30:10.040 --> 00:30:12.639
Where did you get the pen?

439
00:30:12.640 --> 00:30:14.239
Ugh!

440
00:30:14.240 --> 00:30:17.159
Do you think I'm going to take
your eye out with a Biro?

441
00:30:17.160 --> 00:30:18.800
Didn't get anything new anyway.

442
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.559
I've seen this one before.
It must be close.

443
00:30:22.560 --> 00:30:26.239
What does Jesus mean to you.
coming from a religious background?

444
00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:29.199
Did they actually pay you
to make observations like that?

445
00:30:31.080 --> 00:30:32.799
Something big is coming.

446
00:30:32.800 --> 00:30:35.399
Something that will help me find out
who killed her.

447
00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:37.639
But I can't get it in here.

448
00:30:37.640 --> 00:30:38.920
Please.

449
00:30:43.720 --> 00:30:45.360
We'll start in the courtyard.

450
00:30:46.760 --> 00:30:50.319
If you behave.
we'll progress to the lawn.

451
00:30:50.320 --> 00:30:51.520
Deal?

452
00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:54.839
No restraints?

453
00:30:54.840 --> 00:30:56.440
No restraints.

454
00:31:39.720 --> 00:31:41.600
Look. She's new.

455
00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:45.599
I knew you'd bring
something good.

456
00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:46.639
Who is she?

457
00:31:46.640 --> 00:31:48.039
I have no idea.

458
00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:49.879
Maybe someone you met before?

459
00:31:49.880 --> 00:31:51.759
I don't think so.

460
00:31:51.760 --> 00:31:54.199
She's related to my mum somehow...

461
00:31:54.200 --> 00:31:55.400
...to why she died.

462
00:31:56.760 --> 00:31:59.400
Do you want to tell me about that -
your mum dying?

463
00:32:00.840 --> 00:32:02.879
I saw it before.

464
00:32:02.880 --> 00:32:04.480
I warned her.

465
00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:07.039
And she didn't listen.

466
00:32:07.040 --> 00:32:09.079
She did.

467
00:32:09.080 --> 00:32:10.520
We just didn't know when.

468
00:32:12.120 --> 00:32:13.280
Couldn't see that.

469
00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:18.520
I see the way you're looking at me.

470
00:32:19.560 --> 00:32:21.359
Last psych did the same.

471
00:32:21.360 --> 00:32:24.079
"Poor child.
Can't admit what she did."

472
00:32:24.080 --> 00:32:26.239
Is that how it feels? Hard to admit?

473
00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:28.559
Missing the point.
It's not about my feelings.

474
00:32:28.560 --> 00:32:31.039
It's about the fact
that I didn't kill her.

475
00:32:31.040 --> 00:32:32.520
I would never hurt her.

476
00:32:35.240 --> 00:32:39.359
You know. some patients find it hard
to process their guilt.

477
00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:41.679
They try to find ways
of rationalising their actions.

478
00:32:41.680 --> 00:32:43.680
Do you accept your own actions?

479
00:32:45.560 --> 00:32:47.639
It was your fault. wasn't it?

480
00:32:47.640 --> 00:32:50.160
The accident that put you in that?

481
00:32:53.880 --> 00:32:55.199
I know you're upset. Bethany.

482
00:32:55.200 --> 00:32:57.919
but I'd appreciate it if you didn't
speak about my personal life.

483
00:32:57.920 --> 00:33:00.599
Oh. but it's OK to talk about mine?

484
00:33:00.600 --> 00:33:02.239
This is your therapy session.

485
00:33:02.240 --> 00:33:04.119
and I'm just trying
to understand you.

486
00:33:04.120 --> 00:33:05.840
I don't want your understanding.

487
00:33:06.840 --> 00:33:08.760
I want you to get me out of here.

488
00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:26.799
Did she ever request a legal appeal
against her conviction?

489
00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:28.520
Yes. Um...

490
00:33:30.080 --> 00:33:33.319
She did. right at the start.

491
00:33:33.320 --> 00:33:35.119
The lawyer said
she didn't have no grounds.

492
00:33:35.120 --> 00:33:37.839
but she kept asking Dr Morgan
to try again.

493
00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:39.120
And did she?

494
00:33:40.840 --> 00:33:43.359
What happened to Dr Morgan?

495
00:33:43.360 --> 00:33:46.480
Did Dr Morgan have
a mental health crisis?

496
00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:50.039
If I'm expected to give patients
the best support.

497
00:33:50.040 --> 00:33:51.640
I need to know the full history.

498
00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:58.399
Yes. OK. um. Joy Morgan
had a breakdown.

499
00:33:58.400 --> 00:33:59.919
Bethany got too much for her.

500
00:33:59.920 --> 00:34:02.599
And you didn't think
to disclose that?

501
00:34:02.600 --> 00:34:04.199
I didn't think it was relevant.

502
00:34:04.200 --> 00:34:06.679
She repeatedly
denies responsibility.

503
00:34:06.680 --> 00:34:08.839
Did Bethany ever give her
any new evidence

504
00:34:08.840 --> 00:34:10.679
that might form
the basis of an appeal?

505
00:34:10.680 --> 00:34:13.439
Bethany has had
multiple assessments. Gabrielle.

506
00:34:13.440 --> 00:34:15.479
Now. whether you want
to call it narcissism

507
00:34:15.480 --> 00:34:17.879
or antisocial personality disorder.

508
00:34:17.880 --> 00:34:20.159
she is calculating and deceptive.

509
00:34:20.160 --> 00:34:22.319
She has always claimed
she's innocent.

510
00:34:22.320 --> 00:34:25.959
but she's guilty of murder
and very dangerous.

511
00:34:25.960 --> 00:34:28.999
She needs to be on medication
and in a secure unit.

512
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.559
Yeah. and with the Section 41.

513
00:34:30.560 --> 00:34:32.519
she will be -
for the rest of her life.

514
00:34:32.520 --> 00:34:36.479
She'll transfer to the adult unit
at 18 and probably never get out.

515
00:34:36.480 --> 00:34:40.759
So before I work on getting her
to accept responsibility.

516
00:34:40.760 --> 00:34:43.240
I need to be sure
of what I'm dealing with.

517
00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:48.159
It's not normal protocol.
but given the lack of detail

518
00:34:48.160 --> 00:34:51.279
in the notes.
I need to speak to the lawyer.

519
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.679
Sorry about the lift being
out of order.

520
00:35:02.680 --> 00:35:05.639
I'm on the top floor.
so it's intolerably hot.

521
00:35:05.640 --> 00:35:07.760
Anyway. we're better off down here.

522
00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:12.639
Can I ask you. as a lawyer.
did Bethany ask for an appeal?

523
00:35:12.640 --> 00:35:14.599
Right after the conviction.

524
00:35:14.600 --> 00:35:16.519
I had to advise against.

525
00:35:16.520 --> 00:35:19.039
No new evidence has been
brought since then.

526
00:35:19.040 --> 00:35:21.039
Can you talk me through her case?

527
00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:22.759
You know. seeing as I'm here.

528
00:35:22.760 --> 00:35:23.960
Helpful background.

529
00:35:25.480 --> 00:35:28.599
Bethany had been alone
with her mother that day.

530
00:35:28.600 --> 00:35:31.279
Leonard Krall had spent
the morning in meetings.

531
00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:33.439
When he returned home.
he entered the kitchen.

532
00:35:33.440 --> 00:35:35.559
where he found his wife dead
on the floor.

533
00:35:35.560 --> 00:35:38.760
Coroner's report said she must
have been there at least an hour.

534
00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:42.440
Bethany was sitting next to her.
covered in her blood.

535
00:35:44.160 --> 00:35:47.799
Carys's left eye had been
penetrated with a screwdriver.

536
00:35:47.800 --> 00:35:50.599
and the wound was deep
into her brain.

537
00:35:50.600 --> 00:35:51.640
Right.

538
00:35:52.840 --> 00:35:54.279
Leonard's time of arrival home

539
00:35:54.280 --> 00:35:57.479
was corroborated
by the doorbell camera.

540
00:35:57.480 --> 00:35:59.679
But no-one actually saw it happen?

541
00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:00.959
Correct.

542
00:36:00.960 --> 00:36:03.799
We stressed the lack of witnesses.
but the jury weren't convinced.

543
00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:05.639
The doors and windows
were all locked.

544
00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:07.879
No sign of forced entry.

545
00:36:07.880 --> 00:36:10.359
The only people in the house
were Carys and Bethany.

546
00:36:10.360 --> 00:36:12.599
Did you think she was guilty?

547
00:36:12.600 --> 00:36:14.679
She never confessed.

548
00:36:14.680 --> 00:36:16.719
This might sound like
a weird question.

549
00:36:16.720 --> 00:36:20.959
but were there any
drawings involved?

550
00:36:20.960 --> 00:36:24.679
Yeah. The strangest
and most damning thing of all

551
00:36:24.680 --> 00:36:26.839
was that Bethany had drawn
an image of the crime

552
00:36:26.840 --> 00:36:28.480
about a week before it happened.

553
00:36:30.520 --> 00:36:33.680
It's not strictly professional.
but I think you should see it.

554
00:36:40.760 --> 00:36:43.040
The exact way Carys was murdered.

555
00:36:44.840 --> 00:36:46.160
A grisly threat...

556
00:36:47.320 --> 00:36:49.439
...or. as Bethany claimed.

557
00:36:49.440 --> 00:36:51.880
a premonition of an event
that was yet to happen?

558
00:36:59.240 --> 00:37:02.039
As the UK bakes
under record temperatures.

559
00:37:02.040 --> 00:37:04.159
The Climate Front leader.
Anika Drake.

560
00:37:04.160 --> 00:37:07.439
has claimed. "We are on the brink
of a tipping point."

561
00:37:07.440 --> 00:37:10.279
urging the Government to commit
to banning new fossil fuel projects

562
00:37:10.280 --> 00:37:13.199
such as the Rostyre oil field
in Scotland.

563
00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:25.640
Nice to see you! How are you?

564
00:37:28.160 --> 00:37:29.177
- Welcome.
- Hey.

565
00:37:29.178 --> 00:37:31.719
- We've got designated
seating at the front.

566
00:37:31.720 --> 00:37:35.279
I'm... I'm going to just stay here.
Thank you.

567
00:37:35.280 --> 00:37:36.519
Thank you.

568
00:38:09.080 --> 00:38:14.119
- - We stand united.
- We are not alone.

569
00:38:14.120 --> 00:38:17.119
We trust in a higher power.

570
00:38:17.120 --> 00:38:20.200
We are together in our hope.

571
00:38:23.200 --> 00:38:27.200
Welcome. friends.
to this place of peaceful worship.

572
00:38:28.600 --> 00:38:30.439
And it's nice and cool in here. too.
isn't it?

573
00:38:31.640 --> 00:38:33.559
It's wonderful to be
back home again.

574
00:38:33.560 --> 00:38:35.439
When I travel the country.

575
00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:38.559
we say that prayer is
a collective affirmation.

576
00:38:38.560 --> 00:38:41.079
and we need that.
because modern life feels like

577
00:38:41.080 --> 00:38:43.119
an assault sometimes.
doesn't it?

578
00:38:44.360 --> 00:38:46.439
It's too hot.
We're running out of time.

579
00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:50.039
The planet's dying.
We can't just enjoy the sunshine.

580
00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:52.239
Apparently. we have to fear it.

581
00:38:52.240 --> 00:38:55.439
They want to keep us in a doom loop.

582
00:38:55.440 --> 00:38:57.999
Exhausted. Despairing.

583
00:38:58.000 --> 00:39:03.119
"May the God of hope fill you
with all joy and peace."

584
00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:04.799
is what it says in Romans.

585
00:39:04.800 --> 00:39:07.839
It seems to me we should be
looking on the bright side more.

586
00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:12.359
Look at us humans - we make
families. we do great things.

587
00:39:12.360 --> 00:39:16.879
we find solutions. We wake up
and feel the light of a new day.

588
00:39:16.880 --> 00:39:19.639
just like Christ did
2.000 years ago.

589
00:39:19.640 --> 00:39:23.639
The planet was here then
and the planet is still here today.

590
00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:30.839
Dr Fox?

591
00:39:30.840 --> 00:39:32.799
I looked you up.

592
00:39:32.800 --> 00:39:34.839
I take an interest
in my daughter's care.

593
00:39:34.840 --> 00:39:37.639
Are you here for the service.
or in a professional capacity?

594
00:39:37.640 --> 00:39:39.599
I-I. um...

595
00:39:39.600 --> 00:39:42.159
It's OK. You were curious.

596
00:39:42.160 --> 00:39:43.480
I would be too.

597
00:39:44.560 --> 00:39:46.559
Let's talk.

598
00:39:46.560 --> 00:39:48.280
What did you think of the service?

599
00:39:49.360 --> 00:39:51.799
I didn't expect it to be so...

600
00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:53.199
...climate changey.

601
00:39:53.200 --> 00:39:55.399
Well. the young are
constantly served up doom.

602
00:39:55.400 --> 00:39:57.919
Every generation deserves hope.
don't you think?

603
00:39:57.920 --> 00:39:59.519
No.

604
00:39:59.520 --> 00:40:01.319
God isn't really my thing.

605
00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:02.719
Well. the word is very loaded.

606
00:40:02.720 --> 00:40:04.679
Really. it's just a matter
of semantics.

607
00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:06.599
We all yearn for meaning
in our lives.

608
00:40:06.600 --> 00:40:09.079
Pretty radical for a Christian.
to say God's optional.

609
00:40:09.080 --> 00:40:10.919
Well. think of it as a rebranding.

610
00:40:10.920 --> 00:40:14.799
Thanks. Lulu. Different language
for a very different time.

611
00:40:14.800 --> 00:40:16.000
Same heart.

612
00:40:17.720 --> 00:40:20.479
You probably know
she's refused my visits.

613
00:40:20.480 --> 00:40:23.679
I'm not allowed to discuss
what goes on in sessions.

614
00:40:23.680 --> 00:40:25.840
And yet. here you are.
visiting my church.

615
00:40:29.160 --> 00:40:32.120
Is she studying?
How does she pass the time?

616
00:40:33.640 --> 00:40:35.720
She likes art. as you know.

617
00:40:36.880 --> 00:40:38.119
What's she been drawing?

618
00:40:38.120 --> 00:40:40.280
Bethany has a right
to confidentiality.

619
00:40:42.840 --> 00:40:46.120
They started when she was
about 10 or 11. these visions.

620
00:40:48.160 --> 00:40:50.279
Puberty. I suppose.

621
00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:52.639
Dramatics.
Lots of death and despair.

622
00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:55.119
And did she look for things
to validate them?

623
00:40:55.120 --> 00:40:57.319
Oh. yes.
She saw evidence everywhere.

624
00:40:57.320 --> 00:41:00.439
She took coincidences
and twisted them.

625
00:41:00.440 --> 00:41:04.279
Human mind's a powerful thing.
You know that.

626
00:41:04.280 --> 00:41:06.599
We can convince ourselves
of almost anything.

627
00:41:06.600 --> 00:41:11.559
There was nothing real. of course.
Just extreme mental illness.

628
00:41:11.560 --> 00:41:15.280
Carys was distraught.
She tried everything.

629
00:41:17.520 --> 00:41:20.679
In the end. all we could do
was pray for her.

630
00:41:20.680 --> 00:41:22.639
Did you ever think
she'd hurt anyone?

631
00:41:22.640 --> 00:41:25.399
No. not in my wildest dreams.
and definitely not the person

632
00:41:25.400 --> 00:41:28.159
she loved most in the world.
I miss her.

633
00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:30.800
That may surprise you.
after what she did.

634
00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:35.079
She's my only child.

635
00:41:35.080 --> 00:41:37.679
I don't want to lose her
as well as my wife.

636
00:41:37.680 --> 00:41:40.079
I won't give up on her.

637
00:41:40.080 --> 00:41:41.400
You understand that. don't you?

638
00:41:53.360 --> 00:41:54.439
Hiya.

639
00:41:54.440 --> 00:41:57.160
- You forgot.
- No. I got stuff for both of us.

640
00:41:58.680 --> 00:42:02.239
Um. bleach. Haribo.

641
00:42:02.240 --> 00:42:04.559
and a ready meal.

642
00:42:04.560 --> 00:42:06.239
For one.

643
00:42:06.240 --> 00:42:07.639
Nice to share.

644
00:42:07.640 --> 00:42:10.919
So. uh. what do teenagers
worry about. then?

645
00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:12.879
Oh. all sorts.

646
00:42:12.880 --> 00:42:17.239
One patient fixates
on the infinity of space.

647
00:42:17.240 --> 00:42:19.839
another says she can see
the future. so...

648
00:42:19.840 --> 00:42:23.319
Oh! Expect a stranger
with banging culinary skills

649
00:42:23.320 --> 00:42:25.919
coming into your life
in the weeks ahead.

650
00:42:25.920 --> 00:42:26.960
Nice!

651
00:42:30.600 --> 00:42:32.439
Mm! So good.

652
00:42:32.440 --> 00:42:33.032
- Yeah?

653
00:42:33.033 --> 00:42:35.399
- Mm-hm. I forgot what
real food tastes like.

654
00:42:35.400 --> 00:42:38.319
It's lovely to have someone
who appreciates it.

655
00:42:38.320 --> 00:42:40.160
My ex-wife was not a foodie.

656
00:42:41.600 --> 00:42:43.880
Ex-wife? Do tell.

657
00:42:45.920 --> 00:42:49.399
Oh! Shuffles in his seat. reticent.

658
00:42:49.400 --> 00:42:50.799
Oh. my God. please don't do that.

659
00:42:50.800 --> 00:42:53.839
OK. No. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
Go on.

660
00:42:53.840 --> 00:42:56.559
Oh. I don't know. I mean.
she just hated my job. really.

661
00:42:56.560 --> 00:42:58.639
And even when I transferred
to Renewables. it wasn't enough.

662
00:42:58.640 --> 00:43:01.599
because I was still working
for a company that invested in oil.

663
00:43:01.600 --> 00:43:04.919
But. I mean. I don't think anything
was ever going to be enough.

664
00:43:04.920 --> 00:43:08.159
And I guess that just made it
impossible to be together.

665
00:43:08.160 --> 00:43:09.359
Ethical differences.

666
00:43:09.360 --> 00:43:12.319
- Very modern.
- Oh. thank you very much.

667
00:43:12.320 --> 00:43:13.640
How about you?

668
00:43:15.600 --> 00:43:19.279
- Um...
- Shuffles in her seat. reticent...

669
00:43:19.280 --> 00:43:22.959
- Oh. God!
- No. you really don't have to.

670
00:43:22.960 --> 00:43:24.360
No. um...

671
00:43:26.960 --> 00:43:28.400
I was married...

672
00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:33.800
...but my husband died
in the accident.

673
00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:40.999
Fuck.

674
00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:42.720
Let's... Let's not talk about it.

675
00:44:19.680 --> 00:44:21.839
A severe electrical storm
in Lisbon

676
00:44:21.840 --> 00:44:24.919
caused dramatic damage
to Santuario do Cristo-Rei.

677
00:44:24.920 --> 00:44:27.239
the 90-foot tall statue
of Jesus Christ

678
00:44:27.240 --> 00:44:29.079
that overlooks the city.

679
00:44:29.080 --> 00:44:31.599
The storm devastated areas
of southern Lisbon.

680
00:44:31.600 --> 00:44:34.399
with multiple districts evacuated.

681
00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:36.879
Climate scientists are warning
that these sorts

682
00:44:36.880 --> 00:44:40.199
of extreme weather events
will become increasingly common

683
00:44:40.200 --> 00:44:43.159
across southern Europe
as sea temperatures rise.

684
00:44:43.160 --> 00:44:44.799
Look. Emily. look!

685
00:44:44.800 --> 00:44:46.279
- Look!
- Make him go away!

686
00:44:46.280 --> 00:44:48.199
I-I was delivering the news!

687
00:44:48.200 --> 00:44:49.359
He's goading me!

688
00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:51.839
It's going on in Lisbon.
I heard Blanchett talking!

689
00:44:51.840 --> 00:44:53.879
- OK. that's enough.
- I thought you'd want to know!

690
00:44:53.880 --> 00:44:55.919
I told you! Bethany sees things!

691
00:44:55.920 --> 00:44:58.639
You said we could go
on the back lawn if I was good.

692
00:44:58.640 --> 00:45:02.079
and I was good as fucking gold.
wasn't I? Wheels?

693
00:45:02.080 --> 00:45:05.039
It's 40 degrees.
No-one is going outside today.

694
00:45:05.040 --> 00:45:06.400
Ugh!

695
00:45:10.400 --> 00:45:12.040
Sonic told me about the storm.

696
00:45:13.280 --> 00:45:14.760
You know. the Jesus statue.

697
00:45:16.480 --> 00:45:18.519
Don't you get it now?

698
00:45:18.520 --> 00:45:22.959
Ah! No. You're going to say
it's just a coincidence.

699
00:45:22.960 --> 00:45:25.280
- It could be.
- What a nice. comforting thought.

700
00:45:27.360 --> 00:45:28.880
You need to talk to this woman.

701
00:45:31.560 --> 00:45:33.039
I need to talk to her?

702
00:45:33.040 --> 00:45:38.039
Find her. She's somewhere... remote.

703
00:45:38.040 --> 00:45:39.959
Near water. maybe?

704
00:45:39.960 --> 00:45:41.719
And there's a cat.

705
00:45:41.720 --> 00:45:43.679
She has a feral cat.

706
00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:48.199
Whoever she is.
this woman knows something.

707
00:45:48.200 --> 00:45:50.759
Something about why my mum died.

708
00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:52.879
Bethany. I spoke to your lawyer.

709
00:45:52.880 --> 00:45:54.559
because I needed
to get some clarity.

710
00:45:54.560 --> 00:45:55.799
You spoke to Duval?

711
00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:57.999
But there's no grounds
for an appeal.

712
00:45:58.000 --> 00:45:59.239
There's no new evidence.

713
00:45:59.240 --> 00:46:00.879
There is! This woman has it.

714
00:46:00.880 --> 00:46:02.120
- Look...
- Look!

715
00:46:03.920 --> 00:46:06.399
- Bethany.
- You are wasting too much time. - Bethany.

716
00:46:06.400 --> 00:46:09.000
- You need to find her.
- Let go.

717
00:46:10.720 --> 00:46:12.240
I said let go!

718
00:46:36.160 --> 00:46:38.280
- Heya.
- Sorry about that.

719
00:46:39.480 --> 00:46:41.239
Um. I wasn't quick enough.

720
00:46:41.240 --> 00:46:43.880
No. it's fine. it's fine. Sit down.

721
00:46:47.120 --> 00:46:48.880
What do you make of the storm?

722
00:46:50.120 --> 00:46:52.719
I was wondering how that drawing
would actually come true.

723
00:46:52.720 --> 00:46:56.359
Well. the news has been banging on
about extreme weather for months.

724
00:46:56.360 --> 00:46:59.199
Maybe she picked up on that.
made a guess.

725
00:46:59.200 --> 00:47:00.800
She's seen other things. too.

726
00:47:02.080 --> 00:47:04.479
About you.

727
00:47:04.480 --> 00:47:07.400
So. what did the staff know
about me before I got here. then?

728
00:47:08.560 --> 00:47:10.839
Did it get around that I. er...

729
00:47:10.840 --> 00:47:12.679
...that I'd had an accident?

730
00:47:12.680 --> 00:47:13.840
Yes.

731
00:47:15.880 --> 00:47:17.120
People talk.

732
00:47:19.240 --> 00:47:22.520
Yeah. she used it to spook me.
Like she had seen it.

733
00:47:24.440 --> 00:47:25.719
It's a game.

734
00:47:25.720 --> 00:47:28.680
Her visions come true.
time and time again.

735
00:47:30.880 --> 00:47:32.160
You'll see.

736
00:47:34.880 --> 00:47:36.080
Are you religious?

737
00:47:38.480 --> 00:47:43.319
Er. I am. but not
social media spiritualism.

738
00:47:43.320 --> 00:47:45.040
I'm more agnostic myself.

739
00:47:47.040 --> 00:47:49.840
I struggle with the idea
of prophecy. and...

740
00:47:51.400 --> 00:47:52.600
Yeah.

741
00:48:00.280 --> 00:48:02.120
This is Dr Morgan's phone number.

742
00:48:04.160 --> 00:48:06.080
No-one can know I gave you this.

743
00:48:07.360 --> 00:48:09.480
Talk to her. She'll explain.

744
00:48:11.560 --> 00:48:12.880
Thank you.

745
00:48:17.840 --> 00:48:21.399
Sorry I couldn't meet at the house.

746
00:48:21.400 --> 00:48:24.760
My husband can't know
I'm talking to you.

747
00:48:26.440 --> 00:48:28.919
I promised I'd try to move on.

748
00:48:28.920 --> 00:48:30.520
It's about her. isn't it?

749
00:48:31.720 --> 00:48:35.799
Bethany Krall. yeah.
I need to ask you some questions.

750
00:48:35.800 --> 00:48:38.160
I knew you'd turn up
sooner or later.

751
00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:44.400
It's uncanny.

752
00:48:45.520 --> 00:48:47.159
The likeness.

753
00:48:47.160 --> 00:48:49.199
She knew you were coming.

754
00:48:49.200 --> 00:48:51.639
Bethany would draw things
and they'd happen.

755
00:48:51.640 --> 00:48:54.199
Disasters.
pictures of collapsed buildings.

756
00:48:54.200 --> 00:48:56.119
And the next day on the news.
I'd see it.

757
00:48:56.120 --> 00:48:57.680
It happened all the time.

758
00:48:58.840 --> 00:49:00.600
She wanted to break me.

759
00:49:02.560 --> 00:49:04.679
She did break me.

760
00:49:04.680 --> 00:49:06.400
I needed to leave...

761
00:49:07.720 --> 00:49:09.160
...to make way for you.

762
00:49:11.240 --> 00:49:13.519
She believed her powers
could help her find out

763
00:49:13.520 --> 00:49:15.679
what happened to her mother.

764
00:49:15.680 --> 00:49:18.399
And everything led to you.

765
00:49:18.400 --> 00:49:21.160
She believed you would find
the truth.

766
00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:26.119
I know how freaked out you are.
It's OK.

767
00:49:26.120 --> 00:49:27.280
I've been there.

768
00:49:28.440 --> 00:49:30.719
Well. how...

769
00:49:30.720 --> 00:49:32.399
...how is this even possible?

770
00:49:32.400 --> 00:49:35.199
She just seemed to know things
before they happened.

771
00:49:35.200 --> 00:49:37.159
I tried to figure out
how she was doing it.

772
00:49:37.160 --> 00:49:39.239
She didn't have access to any media.

773
00:49:39.240 --> 00:49:41.359
I mean. the other patients...

774
00:49:41.360 --> 00:49:44.999
Well. people do talk.
staff and patients.

775
00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:47.200
Yeah. but she did this drawing
last winter!

776
00:49:49.720 --> 00:49:51.440
She can see the future.

777
00:49:53.080 --> 00:49:54.520
She has to be able to.

778
00:50:08.160 --> 00:50:09.600
Do you recognise her?

779
00:50:12.280 --> 00:50:15.280
You're meant to find her?
Is that it?

780
00:50:16.800 --> 00:50:19.479
Bethany said this woman knows
something about her mum's death.

781
00:50:19.480 --> 00:50:21.160
Well. then. whoever she is. I...

782
00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:24.880
...I fear for her.

783
00:51:08.080 --> 00:51:09.359
Hello?

784
00:51:09.360 --> 00:51:10.679
Dick Carwyn?

785
00:51:10.680 --> 00:51:12.999
It's Dr Gabrielle Fox.

786
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:15.879
We met at that wind farm
event thing.

787
00:51:15.880 --> 00:51:18.079
I'm in the Forge Tavern.

788
00:51:18.080 --> 00:51:20.000
Booze ain't free. but it's cheap.

789
00:51:21.040 --> 00:51:22.520
I'll be here all night.

790
00:51:29.800 --> 00:51:33.239
If I had any sense.
I'd let this lie.

791
00:51:33.240 --> 00:51:36.039
The Kralls have already ruined
my life.

792
00:51:36.040 --> 00:51:37.359
But people should know.

793
00:51:37.360 --> 00:51:39.079
You think people should know what?

794
00:51:39.080 --> 00:51:41.919
I wrote a lot about
The Faith Way early on.

795
00:51:41.920 --> 00:51:44.519
It was mad how quickly they got big.

796
00:51:44.520 --> 00:51:49.039
And when Carys Krall was in London
for some school mental health thing.

797
00:51:49.040 --> 00:51:50.239
I interviewed her.

798
00:51:50.240 --> 00:51:51.799
Mm. What was she like?

799
00:51:51.800 --> 00:51:53.359
Genuinely cared about the kids.

800
00:51:53.360 --> 00:51:55.079
I mean. I didn't go in
for the whole.

801
00:51:55.080 --> 00:51:58.639
you know. God stuff. but. er.
she seemed like a good person.

802
00:51:58.640 --> 00:52:00.159
Where's this going?

803
00:52:00.160 --> 00:52:04.159
Skip forward five years.
and she contacts me out of the blue.

804
00:52:04.160 --> 00:52:06.879
They had a huge following by then.

805
00:52:06.880 --> 00:52:09.719
I mean. literally put faith
back on the map.

806
00:52:09.720 --> 00:52:11.679
And because of that.
they'd stopped engaging

807
00:52:11.680 --> 00:52:14.560
with mainstream press -
they didn't need it.

808
00:52:16.560 --> 00:52:17.880
What did she want?

809
00:52:19.320 --> 00:52:21.319
I... don't know.

810
00:52:21.320 --> 00:52:23.879
She said she had
something to show me.

811
00:52:23.880 --> 00:52:28.039
Asked if she could meet me.
I said. "Yeah. of course."

812
00:52:28.040 --> 00:52:30.599
But then she bailed on me
last minute.

813
00:52:30.600 --> 00:52:33.439
Left a voicemail
saying she couldn't come.

814
00:52:33.440 --> 00:52:38.159
Said she was being followed
and she was scared.

815
00:52:38.160 --> 00:52:41.120
Two days later. she was dead.

816
00:52:48.560 --> 00:52:50.440
The elements will melt
with fervent heat.

817
00:52:52.960 --> 00:52:55.519
The elements will melt
with fervent heat.

818
00:52:55.520 --> 00:52:59.120
Both the earth and the works
that are in it will be burnt up.

819
00:53:00.880 --> 00:53:03.679
We're all looking for meaning.
and it's hard. isn't it.

820
00:53:03.680 --> 00:53:07.119
to know how to find purpose
in the modern world

821
00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:11.359
when there's so much choice.
so much information to navigate?

822
00:53:11.360 --> 00:53:15.519
But if we look to a higher power.
we don't have to seek.

823
00:53:15.520 --> 00:53:17.559
We will be found.

824
00:53:17.560 --> 00:53:19.199
What do you think she wanted?

825
00:53:19.200 --> 00:53:22.279
I don't know. I wish I did.

826
00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:23.719
But put it this way -

827
00:53:23.720 --> 00:53:25.999
I don't for one second believe
she wanted to tell me

828
00:53:26.000 --> 00:53:27.519
she was scared of her daughter.

829
00:53:27.520 --> 00:53:30.599
- You don't?
- No. Why would she come to me?

830
00:53:30.600 --> 00:53:32.759
The elements will melt
with fervent heat...

831
00:53:32.760 --> 00:53:36.359
She would have called someone
to section her. or the police. or...

832
00:53:36.360 --> 00:53:37.999
Well. so what. then?

833
00:53:38.000 --> 00:53:39.559
I covered the case.

834
00:53:39.560 --> 00:53:45.039
kept digging around The Faith Way
until I got called in by my editor.

835
00:53:45.040 --> 00:53:48.879
He tells me the lawyers say
it's a no-go.

836
00:53:48.880 --> 00:53:52.199
Reporting restrictions
because Bethany's a minor.

837
00:53:52.200 --> 00:53:54.839
Fair enough. right?

838
00:53:54.840 --> 00:53:56.439
But then I get dismissed.

839
00:53:56.440 --> 00:53:59.639
Suddenly. no national paper
wants me.

840
00:53:59.640 --> 00:54:02.479
and I'm back in Porth Hen.

841
00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:06.359
having to beg for a job
with the bloody Gazette.

842
00:54:06.360 --> 00:54:08.999
Oh. do you still have the voicemail
from her? Can I hear it?

843
00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:10.759
That's the really weird thing -

844
00:54:10.760 --> 00:54:14.040
my phone stopped working.
All my backups were gone.

845
00:54:15.440 --> 00:54:17.519
It wasn't there.

846
00:54:17.520 --> 00:54:19.319
What. and you think that...?

847
00:54:19.320 --> 00:54:23.519
I KNOW someone wanted
that evidence destroyed.

848
00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:26.279
Let us say a collective
prayer of gratitude

849
00:54:26.280 --> 00:54:29.959
to that higher power
for showing us the way.

850
00:54:29.960 --> 00:54:34.639
for finding our lost souls
and guiding us.

851
00:54:34.640 --> 00:54:35.959
Did you call the police?

852
00:54:35.960 --> 00:54:38.319
Of course. But it was
only my word...

853
00:55:06.440 --> 00:55:10.319
Hey! Let's go outside
and see what's happening.

854
00:55:16.560 --> 00:55:18.599
It's some sort of national warning.

855
00:55:18.600 --> 00:55:21.879
Can everyone please calm down?
I'm sure it's OK.

856
00:55:21.880 --> 00:55:23.839
- Calm down.
- Calm down!

857
00:55:23.840 --> 00:55:27.119
- Help! - Calm down. everyone.
- Please. help!

858
00:55:27.120 --> 00:55:29.919
- Help me! - Are we going to die?
- It's probably just a test.

859
00:55:29.920 --> 00:55:32.799
Stop! Stop! Stop. stop. stop. stop!

860
00:55:39.240 --> 00:55:41.479
- Get out of the way!
- Hey! Watch it. mate.

861
00:55:58.280 --> 00:56:02.399
We're together. and there is nowhere
safer than here.

862
00:56:02.400 --> 00:56:04.439
under this roof.

863
00:56:04.440 --> 00:56:06.399
Join with me.

864
00:56:06.400 --> 00:56:09.519
We stand united.

865
00:56:09.520 --> 00:56:12.960
We are not alone.

866
00:56:14.560 --> 00:56:17.160
We trust in a higher power.

867
00:56:18.880 --> 00:56:22.120
We are together in our hope.

868
00:56:58.960 --> 00:57:02.039
This is The Climate Front.
There is no disaster coming tonight.

869
00:57:02.040 --> 00:57:04.239
but there will be
if we don't act now.

870
00:57:04.240 --> 00:57:07.239
It's time to stop the 1%
putting their own greed

871
00:57:07.240 --> 00:57:09.359
before the needs of the 99%.

872
00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:12.359
Join us for the people's strike
this Thursday.

873
00:57:12.360 --> 00:57:13.919
Don't go to work or school.

874
00:57:13.920 --> 00:57:17.479
Take to the streets to demand people
and the planet before profit.

875
00:57:17.480 --> 00:57:22.040
Together we have the power to change
the system. not the climate.

876
00:57:42.960 --> 00:57:44.439
It's coming.

877
00:57:44.440 --> 00:57:46.159
It's a hoax.

878
00:57:46.160 --> 00:57:48.120
- It's coming.
- We're safe.

879
00:57:49.640 --> 00:57:51.839
We're not safe.

880
00:57:51.840 --> 00:57:52.960
What is coming?

881
00:57:54.200 --> 00:57:56.599
The final link in the chain.

882
00:57:56.600 --> 00:57:57.760
The end.

883
00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:03.240
The Rapture.
